From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vi: no developer log by default

vi_log_lv defaulted to every level, INFO and DBG included. The event
thread prints "VI duration(ms)" at INFO every 100 frames, about every
1.7 s at 60 Hz. That line was 646 of 1141 kernel log lines on the
stand. The server archives the kernel log to the SD card whenever it
changes, checking every minute, so this one line forced a full rewrite
each minute.

vi_log_lv now defaults to ERR, WARN and NOTICE. INFO and DBG remain
available at run time:
echo 31 > /sys/module/cv181x_vi/parameters/vi_log_lv

vi_start_streaming() logged "+" at DBG, and that line served as a
timeline mark when matching resets against server restarts. It is now
"start streaming" at NOTICE, printed once per stream start.

VI_PROFILE stays defined. Besides the timing it also guards
_vi_update_chnRealFrameRate(), which fills u32FrameRate. libkvm reads
that every second (mmf_vi_input_fps) to set the VPSS rate and publish
/run/nanokvm/input_fps.

Both chip variants change alike; only cv181x is built.

diff --git a/interdrv/vi/chip/cv180x/vi.c b/interdrv/vi/chip/cv180x/vi.c
index 9501c42..d7285c6 100644
--- a/interdrv/vi/chip/cv180x/vi.c
+++ b/interdrv/vi/chip/cv180x/vi.c
@@ -53,7 +53,8 @@
 /*******************************************************
  *  Global variables
  ******************************************************/
-u32 vi_log_lv = VI_ERR | VI_WARN | VI_NOTICE | VI_INFO | VI_DBG;
+/* INFO and DBG are developer chatter; set vi_log_lv to 31 to see them. */
+u32 vi_log_lv = VI_ERR | VI_WARN | VI_NOTICE;
 module_param(vi_log_lv, int, 0644);
 
 #ifdef PORTING_TEST //test only
@@ -2944,7 +2945,8 @@ int vi_start_streaming(struct cvi_vi_dev *vdev)
 	enum cvi_isp_raw raw_max = ISP_PRERAW_MAX - 1;
 	int rc = 0;
 
-	vi_pr(VI_DBG, "+\n");
+	/* A timeline mark for logs: NOTICE stays on by default. */
+	vi_pr(VI_NOTICE, "start streaming\n");
 
 	_vi_mempool_reset();
 
diff --git a/interdrv/vi/chip/cv181x/vi.c b/interdrv/vi/chip/cv181x/vi.c
index 9501c42..d7285c6 100644
--- a/interdrv/vi/chip/cv181x/vi.c
